<header><h1>Transactions: Proof</h1></header>
<article>
<p>The source text behind each note on <a href="/R_transactions">Transactions</a>. <b>Explicit</b> sources state the note directly. <b>Implicit</b> sources support it without stating it.</p>

<h2>Notes</h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Players cannot resolve transactions during the strategy phase or the status phase. Players may still negotiate during these phases, but the terms of a deal that involves trade goods cannot be resolved immediately, so that deal is not binding.<sup>2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;You can make transactions during the Action Phase (restricted by neighbors and player turns) and during the Agenda Phase (freely) but not during the Strategy or Status Phases.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When is a deal binding?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Only when its terms resolve immediately.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>The <a href="/F_nomad">Nomad</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Temporal%20Command%20Suite"><i>Temporal Command Suite</i></a> technology and the <a href="/F_yssaril">Yssaril</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Yssaril_Tribes#Breakthrough:~:text=Deepgloom%20Executable"><i>Deepgloom Executable</i></a> breakthrough may allow a transaction at these times.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found. Related site notes (also *): F_nomad Temporal Command Suite and F_yssaril Deepgloom Executable, &ldquo;may allow &hellip; to perform a transaction at a time they usually could not.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>Relic fragments may be traded. Relics themselves cannot be.<sup>1,8</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 94.3: &ldquo;Players can exchange commodities, trade goods, promissory notes, and relic fragments, but cannot exchange other types of cards or tokens.&rdquo; LRR 73.4: &ldquo;Relics cannot be traded.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>8</sup> PoK rulebook, Relics: &ldquo;Relics cannot be exchanged as part of a transaction even though relic fragments can be exchanged.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Captured non&ndash;fighter ships and mechs may be returned to the player that originally owned them as part of a transaction.<sup>1,8</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 17.2a: a captured non-fighter ship or mech is returned &ldquo;If the player who captured the unit agrees to return it as part of a transaction.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>8</sup> PoK rulebook p. 10: &ldquo;A captured non-fighter ship or mech can be returned, as follows: ✦ If the player who captured the unit agrees&rdquo; as part of a transaction.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player becomes neighbors with another player on their turn, they may then perform a transaction with that player.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 94.1: &ldquo;During the active player&rsquo;s turn, they may resolve up to one transaction with each of their neighbors.&rdquo; neighbor status at the time of the transaction is what matters.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>If a player stops being neighbors with another player that they have performed a transaction with this turn, but then become neighbors with that player again later that same turn, they cannot perform a second transaction with that player.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 94.1: &ldquo;During the active player&rsquo;s turn, they may resolve up to one transaction with each of their neighbors.&rdquo; limit is one per neighbor per turn.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <ol><li>The <a href="/F_nomad">Nomad</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Temporal%20Command%20Suite"><i>Temporal Command Suite</i></a> technology may allow a second transaction with the same player in one turn.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does Nomad&rsquo;s Temporal Command Suite faction technology bypass transaction limits? A: Yes, Temporal Command Suite&rsquo;s transaction does not affect performing a second transaction with the same player that turn.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
        <li>A player may perform a transaction during combat with their opponent, even if they are neighbors only in the active system.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Is a transaction an action, and when during a turn can it happen?&rdquo;: &ldquo;the active player can make one with each neighbor at any point in their turn, even mid-combat.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Commodities received in a transaction cannot be given back as part of that same transaction; doing so would require a second transaction.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When do commodities turn into trade goods, and can I give them and get them back in one transaction?&rdquo;: &ldquo;A transaction is one simultaneous exchange, so commodities you receive can&rsquo;t be sent back in it; that would be a second transaction.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>If a player may perform multiple actions on their turn, they may still only resolve one transaction with each of their neighbors.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Is a transaction an action, and when during a turn can it happen?&rdquo;: &ldquo;the active player can make one with each neighbor at any point in their turn.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 94.1: &ldquo;During the active player&rsquo;s turn, they may resolve up to one transaction with each of their neighbors.&rdquo; limit is per turn, not per action.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If an agenda is discarded and replaced with another, players who resolved a transaction during the discarded agenda may resolve another transaction during the replacement agenda.<sup>5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling, asked whether a replacement agenda refreshes &ldquo;the &lsquo;transaction allowance&rsquo;&rdquo;: &ldquo;I would also say that they could perform new transactions.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
</article>
